{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>And he was there with HaShem forty days and forty nights, and he wrote upon the tablets</b> — Scripture says that Moses was there at the top of the mountain forty days and forty nights, and he wrote there upon the tablets. And according to the opinion of our Sages (in Midrash Tanchuma, Ki Tisa 31), the meaning of the verse is that he was there with HaShem forty days and forty nights at the time He wrote upon the tablets the words of this second covenant; but forty other days he had stood there beforehand to pray concerning the entire matter of his supplication, as he said (Exodus 33:12), \"See, You say to me, 'Bring up this people'\" — and concerning them it is stated in Deuteronomy (Deuteronomy 9:25), \"And I fell down before HaShem the forty days and the forty nights that I fell down, because HaShem had said He would destroy you.\" Here Scripture did not specify how many were the days of this supplication and prayer, for it is already known from the time of his ascent up the mountain until his descent to hew the latter tablets. But it recounted that the matter of the second tablets was like the entire matter of the first ones — in the writing of Elohim and in the days he stood there before HaShem — so that one should not think that since he had already learned the Torah the first time, he would not now need to stand there a long time." "And the sense of <b>and he wrote upon the tablets</b> is that HaShem wrote, and it does not revert to Moses, for thus He said (Exodus 34:1), \"And I will write upon the tablets,\" and likewise in Deuteronomy (Deuteronomy 10:3–4), \"And I hewed two tablets of stone like the first ones, and I went up the mountain, and the two tablets were in my hand, and He wrote upon the tablets according to the first writing.\" And since it says \"according to the first writing,\" we know that they were written by the finger of Elohim, and the meaning of \"And I will write\" (Exodus 34:1) will be \"with My finger,\" and you already know the meaning of \"finger\" of the hand (Ramban on Exodus 14:31)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:53.806119684Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}